  For F = RG(n, k) or F = RG(n), w1 acts trivially since any RG-word f satisfies f (1) = 1. Thus,
w = wn ◦ · · · w3 ◦ w2 on these families of functions. So when we consider generalized toggle orders we
define wπ = wπ(n) ◦ · · · ◦ wπ(3) ◦ wπ(2) where π is a permutation of {2, 3, . . . , n}.
